//@version=6
indicator("UCTPROBE_VW_TF_FORMAT_DATE_TOKENS", overlay = true)

// PROVENANCE: written 2026-11-19 (Q-TF-W2-a / Q-TF-W2-b, docs/pine/capture-queue-2026-11-20-text-format.md). Our probe, licence `probe`.
// NEVER COMPILED ON TRADINGVIEW: a line that does not compile IS a reading - record the error text and the line.
// ⛔ A pattern letter TradingView does not hold may STOP the script with a runtime error: then the error text
// is the reading, recorded with the row it names.
//
// ─── W2: `str.format("{0,date,P}", t)` - THE PATTERN LETTERS, AT FIXED INSTANTS ───
//
// The committed capture vw-w3-format-date-spy-1d-2026-11-16 printed 2024-03-05 14:07:09 UTC as
// "05 March 2024, 14:07:09" on AMEX:SPY (an exchange in New York): UTC, not the exchange's zone. This battery
// asks every common letter at six instants and on the bar's own times, on a US equity and on a crypto pair.
//
// Table 1, one row per pattern (D01-D23 as `{0,date,P}`, D24 a time element, D25 the manual's ISO example);
// one column per instant:
//   iA         2024-03-05 14:07:09 UTC, the instant of vw-w3-format-date (continuity)
//   iB         2024-07-04 03:02:01.045 UTC: summer, one-digit hour / minute / second
//   iC         2023-12-31 23:59:59.999 UTC: the year's last millisecond, a Sunday
//   iD         2021-01-01 00:00:00 UTC: midnight, a Friday
//   iE         1969-12-31 23:59:59 UTC: before 1970, a negative timestamp
//   iN         2024-11-11 12:00:00 UTC: noon
//   time       the bar's opening time (the exchange session's open on a daily chart)
//   time_close the bar's closing time
// Table 2: M01-M12 each month's names on its 15th (MMMM|MMM|MM); W01-W07 each weekday, 2024-03-04 (a Monday) to
// 2024-03-10 (EEEE|EEE|dd).
//
// CAPTURE: AMEX:SPY 1D and BITSTAMP:BTCUSD 1D; AMEX:SPY 60 for the intraday bar times. Inputs at defaults.

